Third-party components
======================

This repository redistributes the third-party material listed below.
Each item retains its own copyright and license; the MIT grant above does
not apply to these files.

1. libsidplayfp  —  GNU GPL v2 or later
   Files:
     tools/libsidplayfp-overlay/    (committed headers/sources)
     tools/siddump.cpp              (original SIDfinity code that links libsidplayfp)
   Copyright 2011-2025 Leandro Nini <drfiemost@users.sourceforge.net>
   Copyright 2007-2010 Antti Lankila
   Copyright 2000-2001 Simon White
   and the libsidplayfp contributors.
   Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
   Full license text: tools/libsidplayfp-overlay/COPYING

   tools/siddump.cpp is original SIDfinity code, but it includes and links
   libsidplayfp; the resulting binary is a combined work distributed under
   the GPL v2. tools/build.sh additionally clones and builds the full
   libsidplayfp library and the xa65 assembler (both GPL v2) into gitignored
   directories — those build trees are not part of this distribution.

2. GoatTracker  —  GNU GPL v2  (in deprecated/)
   Files:
     deprecated/gt2_pipeline/GoatTracker_2.65/ … GoatTracker_2.77/
   Copyright Lasse Öörni and the GoatTracker contributors.
   Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2.
   Full license text: each tree's "copying" file
   (e.g. deprecated/gt2_pipeline/GoatTracker_2.77/copying).

   These trees also bundle:
     - reSID, Copyright Dag Lem and contributors — GNU GPL v2
       (deprecated/gt2_pipeline/GoatTracker_*/src/resid/)
     - SDL (sdl.dll), the Simple DirectMedia Layer — GNU LGPL
       (see each tree's readme_sdl.txt for the LGPL notice and source URL)

   PLAYROUTINE EXCEPTION. The playroutine sources src/player.s and
   src/altplayer.s within each GoatTracker tree — and
   deprecated/old_player/sidfinity_gt2.asm, which is derived from them —
   carry the author's explicit notice:

     "This playroutine source code does not fall under the GPL license!
      Use it, or song binaries created from it freely for any purpose,
      commercial or noncommercial."

   Some SIDfinity player-code-generation work (notably the deprecated V2
   code generator under deprecated/v2_codegen/ and deprecated/old_player/)
   was originally based on this GoatTracker V2 playroutine.

3. SIDdecompiler  —  MIT
   File:
     pipelines/hubbard/docs/siddecompiler_full_source.cpp
   Copyright (c) 2017 Stein Pedersen
   Licensed under the MIT License (the copyright and permission notice are
   retained in the file's header). Source:
   https://github.com/Galfodo/SIDdecompiler

4. Third-party Commodore 64 software and SID music  —  preservation
   The files below are the property of their respective authors. They are
   included solely for research, interoperability, and preservation in the
   spirit of the High Voltage SID Collection (HVSC). They are NOT covered by
   the MIT license above, are provided with no warranty, and will be removed
   on request by a rights holder.

   C64 music-editor / player binaries:
     pipelines/future_composer/artifacts/*.prg     (Future Composer family)
     pipelines/john_player/docs/src/**             (John Player editor)
     pipelines/music_assembler/docs/*.prg          (Music Assembler / Triad)
     pipelines/soundmonitor/docs/vendor/*.prg      (Sound Monitor)
     pipelines/dmc/docs/*.bin                       (DMC player code)
     deprecated/dmc_wip/dmc/binaries/*.prg          (Demo Music Creator)

   SID tunes and SIDfinity rebuilds of copyrighted compositions:
     deprecated/gt2_grading/demo/*.sid
     deprecated/usf1_pipelines/*/build/*.sid
     pipelines/hubbard/five_title_tunes/work_subs/*.sid

5. HVSC catalogue metadata
   hvsc84.db contains catalogue metadata only — file paths, tune titles,
   author names, song lengths, and content hashes derived from the High
   Voltage SID Collection (https://www.hvsc.c64.org/). It contains no SID
   audio and no binary tune data. The HVSC collection itself is not included
   in this repository.
